<h1>Multi-Site Scanning Procedure</h1>
<div class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center">
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3"></div>
<p>Once all preparation has been done scanning may commence. A step by step procedure is given here.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Scanning procedure</p>
<p>In order to be successful whilst scanning the appropriate procedure must be followed. The procedure has 3 main stages:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Setup of the required scanning area</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Measuring the position of a set of floor mounted datum cones</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Data capture, using one of 6 available Scanning Sites</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="stepstitle">Determination of scanning area</p>
<p class="whs4">The scanning area must be of sufficient size to move the scanner to the necessary locations.</p>
<p class="whs4">The number of datum cones and position will depend on the size of the car (scanning area) and the measuring radius R of the localiser. In this example, the car can be scanned using 16 datum cones with a FARO 12' localiser.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Move the car into position</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Mark a box around the car, about 0.5m larger than the car</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Remove the car</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span style="font-size:10pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Mark the two measurement positions M1 and M2 on the centre line of the rectangle using the tape. They are distance R apart and centrally located in the scanning box.</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><img id="_x0000_i1026" src="../../Images/multisite_pic2.jpg" width="325px" height="254px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head-steptitle">Marking out of scanning sites</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Mark out the scanning site correctly to avoid unnecessary errors later whilst scanning.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The measuring positions M1 and M2 are only required for establishing the overall positions of all the cones. When the car is driven back in, they are no longer accessible.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">During the data capture the localiser will be positioned at one of the 6 available Scanning sites (S1 to S6) where 3 of the previously measured datum cones can be accessed by the localiser and used to establish a co-ordinate system.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Mark out the scanning sites S1 to S6 as shown using tape:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><img id="_x0000_i1027" src="../../Images/multisite_pic1.jpg" width="325px" height="240px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head-steptitle">Placement of datum cones</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The datum cones must be positioned correctly to ensure optimum scanning.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Position the cones as shown (the precise position is not important, as they will be accurately measured later) in an orderly sequence</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Double check the positions of the cones, then fix them with the glue gun</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Wait for the glue to dry, then use the numbered discs to number them in sequence</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="stepstitle">Measurement of datum cones (position M1)</p>
<p>The positions of the datum cones at position M1 are now registered.</p>
<p>Now you will need to run <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>KUBE</b></span>.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Set up the arm at position M1 - the sensor does NOT need to be installed at this point</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Open a new document</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">The document should already be in <span class="Mode">Multi-Site</span> mode, this is indicated by <span class="Mode">Single-Site</span> shown in the scanning menu.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Select <span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Set-up</b></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">A prompt appears to place the arm in the start position, Press 'A' to continue.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">A grid appears with numbers 1 to 31, select appropriate disk number.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="../../Images/mulitsite_scanning.gif" width="332px" height="350px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Place the touch probe in the correct datum cone</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Button 'B' to switch pause off and collect data of position of cone.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Make sure the correct cone number is always entered - failure to do so will make the scan impossible.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Capture a large number of points with the arm at a variety of different angles</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Follow the on screen instructions</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Repeat this procedure for all 11 cones within scanning range</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Select <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'New Arm Position'</b></span> within the grid</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="stepstitle">Measurement of datum cones (position M2)</p>
<p>The positions of the datum cones at position M2 are next registered.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Move the arm to position M2</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12.0pt;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Follow the same procedure as described above to digitise the ALL 11 cones within the reach of the arm</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Warning" id="P1">Make sure the correct cone number is always entered - failure to do so will make the scan impossible.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="stepstitle">Scanning</p>
<p class="whs4">Now scanning can take place as normal</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Move the scanning equipment out of the way.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Move the car in position</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Place the arm at one of the scanning sites</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Select 'New position' within the scanning menu</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Follow the on screen instructions digitising the positions of at least 3 cones.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Scan as normal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
